{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Has sworn.</b> This too is an indication that this prophecy concerns the future, for HaShem has sworn, which is a decree without condition. The sense of \"by His right hand\" is like \"His might,\" which stands forever. The reason for mentioning \"by His right hand\" in this place is that no man will be able to take your grain by force:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 62, :notes {0 "Resolved גם זה as 'this too,' connecting to a prior argument about the prophecy's future orientation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:40.783744798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}